main.py, ints.py, comprehension.py and concat.py in one program. Each part
takes about a second; together they did not finish in 300 s (4 s before
asserts became `assert; assume`, PLR 7.3). The assumed conditions of
`x in s` (line 19), `len(t) == 2` (line 25) and `d == {"a1", "b1"}`
(line 36) make the bit-vector refinement's SAT query (about 170000
variables and 610000 clauses) hard: assuming any one of these three alone
after its assert takes over 30 s, assuming any other one alone about 2 s.
